 "_about": "The remake's silver-rupee rooms (dungeons plugin, tools/rando/parity/_dungeons_silver.py; evidence). Each OoTR puzzle (vendor/ootr World.silver_rupee_puzzles, vanilla layouts) is one remake room: its counter placement(s) (Obj_silverRupeeCounter*, which links its 5 Obj_RupeeToken_Silver placements and counts the linked tokens still alive; the counter itself is the glass/gate the set opens) and the 5 token placements, in the order of the counter's Links. Gerudo Training Ground's boulder room (OoTR's Slopes) has two counters whose tokens stand at the same 5 spots (one set per side the room is entered from; either set's completion sets GerudoTrainingGround_Dungeon_Room02_SilverRupee, which deletes both groups): the two tokens at one spot share a spot. 80 spots for OoTR's 80 silver rupees, 85 token placements. Positions are the placements' Translate (x, y, z). 'give': 'window' for the underwater room: its spots give with GetPouchContent's get window (what Dm_SY_Get_WithoutPlayer shows in the water) instead of Link holding the item up. 'room' is the counter's DefaultDungeonRoomIndex; 'done' the persistent Bools that room's logic modules read once the set is complete (each exists in GameDataList as a saved Bool: ResetTypeValue 8, SaveFileIndex 0); 'opens' what the counter (the barrier) guards.",
